module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.HigherDegree.ComplementCechModuleComparison
public import
StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.CechOfSheavesOfModules.ModuleValuedAlternatingComparison

/-!
# The ordered Čech complex of the standard covering is the algebraic one, `A`-linearly

Let `A` be a commutative ring, let `I = (f₁, …, f_r)` be generated by a finite family and let
`U = Spec A \ V(I)`, covered by the basic opens `D(f_i)`. The degreewise comparison
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.ordCochainToCechTerm` of the ordered Čech complex of that covering with
the extended alternating Čech complex `C^•(f₁, …, f_r; M)` is `A`-linear, where the ordered Čech
cochains are the ones of the slice site over `U` — modules over `Γ(U, 𝒪)` — with their scalars
restricted to `A` along `Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementOpenScalars`. Consequently
`H^p(U, M̃) ≅ H^{p+1}_{V(I)}(M)` as `A`-modules for every `p ≥ 1`, which is clause (2) of
[Stacks, Tag 0DWR] for `M̃`, with `I` finitely generated and `A` arbitrary.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.ordCochainModuleEquivCechTerm` — **the degreewise comparison as an
  `A`-linear equivalence** `Č^p(𝒰, M̃) ≃ₗ[A] C^{p+1}(f₁, …, f_r; M)`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.ordCechModuleHomologyIso` — **the comparison on cohomology, as
  `A`-modules**, in degrees above zero.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementOpenScalars_smul_moduleSections` — **the structure-sheaf
  action of a scalar on local sections of `M̃` is the direct action.**
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.ordCochainToCechTerm_smul` — the degreewise comparison is `A`-linear.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.nonempty_cechStandardModuleHomology_iso_extendedCechHomology` — the
  Čech cohomology of the standard covering, read over `A`, is the cohomology of
  `C^•(f₁, …, f_r; M)` one degree up, as `A`-modules.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomologySequence.nonempty_complementCohomologyBase_iso_localCohomologyModule` —
  `H^p(U, M̃) ≅ H^{p+1}_{V(I)}(M)` for `p ≥ 1`, `A`-linearly, for a finitely generated ideal of an
  arbitrary ring.

## Implementation notes

Neither of the two module structures involved is an instance — the slice-site action
`Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf.sectionsModuleOfLE` and the cochainwise action
`Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf.ordCochainModule` are `def`s, since the covered open `U` is not
determined by the open `W` or by the index tuple. They are introduced by `letI` in the
statements, with the type ascribed at the submodule or at the cochain type rather than at the
presheaf-section type: instance search runs at reducible transparency, where
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.associatedAbPresheaf` does not unfold, so a scalar action written at
`ToType ((associatedAbPresheaf M).obj (op W))` is not found.

`AddEquiv.toLinearEquiv` cannot be used to upgrade
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.ordCochainEquivCechTerm`: its `[Module R M]` argument is synthesized at
the source type as the `AddEquiv` spells it, which is the abelian-group-valued cochain object and
carries no `A`-action. The `A`-linear equivalence is assembled by structure update instead, which
elaborates against the expected type and so takes the restriction-of-scalars action from it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DWR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DWR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A6R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A6R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A6T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A6T)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G71](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G71)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01FI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01FI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01FJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01FJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01FM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01FM)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf

attribute [local instance] ModuleCat.hasLimitsOfSize
attribute [local instance] AddCommGrpCat.hasLimitsOfSize

universe u

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A) (I : Ideal A)
  (hIf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I) (M : ModuleCat.{u} A)

/-! ### The structure-sheaf action of a scalar is the direct action -/

/-- **The structure-sheaf action of a scalar on local sections of `M̃` is the direct action.**
Let `W ⊆ U = Spec A \ V(I)` be open. A scalar `a ∈ A` acts on the locally fractional sections of
`M` over `W` in two ways: through the ring of functions `Γ(U, 𝒪)`, along the structure map
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementOpenScalars`, which is the action the slice site over `U`
carries; and directly, `W`-component by `W`-component, which is the action of the submodule
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.moduleSections`. The two agree. -/
theorem complementOpenScalars_smul_moduleSections {W : Opens (PrimeSpectrum.Top A)}
    (h : W ≤ complementZeroLocus A I) (a : A) (t : moduleSections M W) :
    letI : Module (SectionRing (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf
        (complementZeroLocus A I)) (moduleSections M W) :=
      sectionsModuleOfLE (complementZeroLocus A I) (associatedSheaf A M) h
    complementOpenScalars I a • t = a • t :=
  Subtype.ext (funext fun x =>
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul (LocalizedModule x.1.asIdeal.primeCompl A) a (t.1 x))

/-! ### The degreewise comparison is `A`-linear -/

/-- **The degreewise comparison of the ordered Čech complex of the standard covering with the
extended alternating Čech complex is `A`-linear.** -/
theorem ordCochainToCechTerm_smul (p : ℕ) (a : A)
    (s : ToType ((orderedCechStandard f M).X p)) :
    letI : Module (SectionRing (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf
        (complementZeroLocus A I)) (ToType ((orderedCechStandard f M).X p)) :=
      ordCochainModule (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
        (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf) (associatedSheaf A M) p
    ordCochainToCechTerm f M p (complementOpenScalars I a • s) =
      a • ordCochainToCechTerm f M p s := by
  refine DirectSum.ext fun T => ?_
  obtain ⟨σ, rfl⟩ : ∃ σ, ordIndexEquiv p σ = T :=
    ⟨(ordIndexEquiv p).symm T, (ordIndexEquiv p).apply_symm_apply T⟩
  refine (cechComponent_ordCochainToCechTerm f M p _ σ).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (cechStandardTupleSectionsEquiv f M σ.1)
    (ordCochain_smul_apply (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
      (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf) (associatedSheaf A M) p
      (complementOpenScalars I a) s σ)) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (cechStandardTupleSectionsEquiv f M σ.1)
    (complementOpenScalars_smul_moduleSections
      (W := CechCochains.inter (cechStandardOpen f) σ.1) I M
      (cechInter_le_covered (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
        (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf) σ.1) a (s σ))) ?_
  refine ((cechStandardTupleSectionsEquiv f M σ.1).map_smul a (s σ)).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z : Cech.cechMod f (M : Type _) (ordIndexEquiv p σ).1 => a • z)
    (cechComponent_ordCochainToCechTerm f M p s σ).symm) ?_
  exact ((cechComponent f M (p + 1) (ordIndexEquiv p σ)).map_smul a
    (ordCochainToCechTerm f M p s)).symm

/-! ### The comparison on cohomology, `A`-linearly -/

/-- **The degreewise comparison, as an `A`-linear equivalence**: the degree-`p` ordered Čech
cochains of the standard covering, read over `A`, are the degree-`p+1` term of the extended
alternating Čech complex `C^•(f₁, …, f_r; M)`. -/
def ordCochainModuleEquivCechTerm (p : ℕ) :
    ToType ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u} (complementOpenScalars I)).obj
        ((orderedModuleComplex (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
          (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
          (associatedSheaf A M)).X p)) ≃ₗ[A] Cech.cechTerm f (M : Type _) (p + 1) :=
  { (ordCochainEquivCechTerm f M p) with
    map_smul' := ordCochainToCechTerm_smul f I hIf M p
    invFun := (ordCochainEquivCechTerm f M p).symm
    left_inv := (ordCochainEquivCechTerm f M p).left_inv
    right_inv := (ordCochainEquivCechTerm f M p).right_inv }

/-- The degreewise comparison, as an isomorphism of `A`-modules. -/
def ordCechModuleXIso (p : ℕ) :
    (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u} (complementOpenScalars I)).obj
        ((orderedModuleComplex (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
          (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf) (associatedSheaf A M)).X p) ≅
      (_root_.Cech.cechComplex f (M : Type _)).X (p + 1) :=
  (ordCochainModuleEquivCechTerm f I hIf M p).toModuleIso

/-- The degreewise comparison of `A`-modules is the map
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.ordCochainToCechTerm` on elements. -/
theorem ordCechModuleXIso_hom_apply (p : ℕ)
    (s : ToType ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u} (complementOpenScalars I)).obj
      ((orderedModuleComplex (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
        (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf) (associatedSheaf A M)).X p))) :
    ModuleCat.Hom.hom (ordCechModuleXIso f I hIf M p).hom s =
      ordCochainToCechTerm f M p s := rfl

/-- The degreewise comparison of `A`-modules commutes with the differentials. -/
theorem ordCechModuleXIso_comm (p : ℕ) :
    (ordCechModuleXIso f I hIf M p).hom ≫
        (_root_.Cech.cechComplex f (M : Type _)).d (p + 1) (p + 2) =
      (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u} (complementOpenScalars I)).map
          ((orderedModuleComplex (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
            (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
            (associatedSheaf A M)).d p (p + 1)) ≫
        (ordCechModuleXIso f I hIf M (p + 1)).hom := by
  rw [_root_.Cech.cechComplex_d f (M : Type _) (p + 1), orderedModuleComplex_d]
  ext s
  exact (ordCochainToCechTerm_ordD f M p s).symm

/-- The three-term truncation of the ordered Čech complex of the standard covering over `A`
around degree `q + 1` is the three-term truncation of the extended alternating Čech complex
around degree `q + 2`. -/
def ordCechModuleShortComplexIso (q : ℕ) :
    ((orderedModuleComplex (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
          (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
          (associatedSheaf A M)).sc' q (q + 1) (q + 2)).map
        (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u} (complementOpenScalars I)) ≅
      (_root_.Cech.cechComplex f (M : Type _)).sc' (q + 1) (q + 2) (q + 3) :=
  ShortComplex.isoMk (ordCechModuleXIso f I hIf M q) (ordCechModuleXIso f I hIf M (q + 1))
    (ordCechModuleXIso f I hIf M (q + 2))
    (ordCechModuleXIso_comm f I hIf M q) (ordCechModuleXIso_comm f I hIf M (q + 1))

/-- **The Čech cohomology of the standard covering is the cohomology of the extended alternating
Čech complex, shifted by one, `A`-linearly.** In every degree `q + 1 ≥ 1` the degree-`q+1`
cohomology of the ordered Čech complex of the covering of `U = Spec A \ V(f₁, …, f_r)` by the
basic opens, read over `A`, is the degree-`q+2` cohomology of `C^•(f₁, …, f_r; M)` as an
`A`-module. This is the `A`-linear form of
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.orderedCechHomologyIsoCechComplexHomology`. -/
def ordCechModuleHomologyIso (q : ℕ) :
    (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u} (complementOpenScalars I)).obj
        ((orderedModuleComplex (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
          (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
          (associatedSheaf A M)).homology (q + 1)) ≅
      (_root_.Cech.cechComplex f (M : Type _)).homology (q + 2) :=
  letI : (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u} (complementOpenScalars I)).PreservesHomology :=
    restrictScalars_preservesHomology (complementOpenScalars I)
  (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u} (complementOpenScalars I)).mapIso
      ((orderedModuleComplex (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
        (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
        (associatedSheaf A M)).homologyIsoSc' q (q + 1) (q + 2) (by simp) (by simp)) ≪≫
    (ShortComplex.mapHomologyIso
      (S := (orderedModuleComplex (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
        (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
        (associatedSheaf A M)).sc' q (q + 1) (q + 2))
      (F := ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u} (complementOpenScalars I))).symm ≪≫
    ShortComplex.homologyMapIso (ordCechModuleShortComplexIso f I hIf M q) ≪≫
    ((_root_.Cech.cechComplex f (M : Type _)).homologyIsoSc' (q + 1) (q + 2) (q + 3)
      (by simp) (by simp)).symm

/-! ### The module-valued Čech comparison of the standard covering -/

/-- **The Čech cohomology of the standard covering is the cohomology of the extended alternating
Čech complex, shifted by one, as `A`-modules.** For `p = q + 1 ≥ 1` the degree-`p` cohomology of
the Čech complex of [Stacks, Tag 01EP] of the covering of `U = Spec A \ V(I)` by the basic opens
`D(f_i)`, with its scalars restricted from `Γ(U, 𝒪)` to `A`, is the degree-`p+1` cohomology of
`C^•(f₁, …, f_r; M)`. -/
theorem nonempty_cechStandardModuleHomology_iso_extendedCechHomology (q : ℕ) :
    Nonempty ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u} (complementOpenScalars I)).obj
        ((Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf.cechComplex.{u, u, u, u} (complementZeroLocus A I)
            (cechStandardOpen f)
            (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
            (associatedSheaf A M)).homology (q + 1)) ≅
      (extendedCechComplex f M).homology (((q + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + 1)) := by
  have hdeg : (((q + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + 1) = (q : ℤ) + 2 := by push_cast; ring
  rw [hdeg]
  exact ⟨(ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u} (complementOpenScalars I)).mapIso
      (orderedCechHomologyModuleIso (complementZeroLocus A I) (cechStandardOpen f)
        (complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf) (associatedSheaf A M)
        (q + 1)).symm ≪≫
    ordCechModuleHomologyIso f I hIf M q ≪≫ (extendedCechHomologyIso f M q).symm⟩

end Stacks.LocalCohomology

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomologySequence

variable {A : CommRingCat.{u}}

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0DWR] (2) for `M̃`, `A`-linearly, for a finitely generated ideal of an
arbitrary commutative ring.** Let `I` be a finitely generated ideal of a commutative ring `A`, let
`U = Spec A \ V(I)` and let `M` be an `A`-module. For every `p = q + 1 ≥ 1` the `A`-module
`H^p(U, M̃)` is the local cohomology `H^{p+1}_{V(I)}(M)`.

The source only asserts that the two modules are isomorphic, so the conclusion is nonemptiness
of the type of isomorphisms. -/
theorem nonempty_complementCohomologyBase_iso_localCohomologyModule
    (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG) (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (q : ℕ) :
    Nonempty (complementCohomologyBase I M (q + 1) ≅
      Stacks.LocalCohomology.localCohomologyModule A I hI M (((q + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + 1)) :=
  nonempty_complementCohomologyBase_iso_localCohomologyModule_of_cech I hI M (q + 1)
    (fun f hIf =>
      Stacks.LocalCohomology.nonempty_cechStandardModuleHomology_iso_extendedCechHomology
        f I hIf M q)

end Stacks.LocalCohomologySequence


end
